{
  "requirement": "Usage MUST record each provider request's outcome and available input/output\ntoken counts, including retries, with cached or reasoning-token counts when\nprovided. Missing measurements MUST be recorded as unavailable, not zero.\nRun totals MUST include request and tool-call counts by tool, elapsed time, and\navailable token usage, identifying incomplete totals without double counting\nprovider counters that overlap.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The sources satisfy `usage_requests`. I found no unmarked implementation code or unspecified behaviour, and the tests cover the main cases. One assumption I could not check is noted at the end.\n\n**Per-request outcome and tokens, including retries**\n- `assess` in `src/authoring/mod.rs` calls `usage.begin_request()` before every provider attempt and `usage.end_request()` after it. This covers retries, backoff and timed-out attempts.\n- `begin_request` and `end_request` in `src/authoring/usage.rs` push one `RequestUsage` per attempt. Each records an outcome (`unfinished`, `completed`, `failed`, or `cancelled` via `finish`), its elapsed time and its token counts.\n- `bedrock_sdk_config` disables SDK-internal retries so that every attempt appears in the ledger. The Ollama path in `RigProvider::connect` has no hidden retry layer. Both are marked `{impl}`.\n\n**Missing measurements recorded as unavailable**\n- `TokenCounts` stores `Option<u64>` for input, output, cached-input, cache-creation and reasoning counts. `from_usage` maps the provider's `Usage` directly, so absent counters stay `None` rather than becoming 0.\n- A failed or abandoned request gets `TokenCounts::default()`: all counters `None` and `complete=false`.\n- Tests assert the `null` values (`is_null()`) and the distinction between an explicit 0 and a missing counter. In `partial_failure_retains_available_totals_and_optional_measurements`, `cached_input(0)` is summed as 0 while `reasoning` stays null.\n\n**Run totals**\n- `tool()` and `skipped_tool()` keep `tool_calls` per tool name plus `tool_call_count`. `tool_name` maps unrecognised names to `unknown`, so model text never leaks into the log.\n- `request_count` and `elapsed_ms` are updated at begin, end and finish. `finish` also records elapsed time for a cancelled in-flight request.\n- `TokenCounts::sum` and `sum_counter` aggregate per counter and keep partial subtotals when some requests lack a measurement. `complete` is true only if every request has input and output and the optional counters are measured consistently.\n- Cached, cache-creation and reasoning counts are summed separately and never added into the input or output totals. This is the \"no double counting of overlapping counters\" requirement.\n\n**Tests**\n- `token_totals_keep_subsets_separate_and_missing_counters_unknown` covers subtotals that do not double count, the in-flight incomplete state, and a later failed request leaving the total incomplete.\n- `partial_failure_retains_available_totals_and_optional_measurements` covers mixed optional counters.\n- `cancelled_request_persists_elapsed_time_and_incomplete_totals` covers the cancelled outcome and elapsed time.\n- `tool_outcomes_are_distinct_and_unknown_names_do_not_leak_model_text` covers tool counts by tool.\n- `throttled_requests_retry_unchanged_and_record_every_attempt` (8 failed attempts and 1 completed), `unanswered_requests_are_abandoned_and_retried` and the retry-after-tool-turn test in `mod.rs` cover retries.\n- The CLI integration tests check the end-to-end ledger: Ollama token sums of 22 and 14, Bedrock sums of 38 and 10, request counts, tool counts and failures, and failed runs from denied reads.\n\n**Not verified**\n- I could not inspect the upstream Rig conversion for Ollama or Bedrock. It might turn a missing counter into 0 before it reaches this code.\n- `sum` assumes cache and reasoning counters are subsets of input and output, and never adds them in.\n- Neither assumption is contradicted anywhere in the supplied sources.",
  "inputs": [
